To set up notifications for a failed backup, follow these steps:

1. **Modify Your Backup Script**: Edit your backup script to include error handling. For example:
   ```sql
   BEGIN TRY
       BACKUP DATABASE Database1 TO DISK = 'C:\Users\YourUsername\OneDrive\Backups\Database1.bak' WITH INIT;
   END TRY
   BEGIN CATCH
       EXEC msdb.dbo.sp_send_dbmail
       @profile_name = 'YourProfile',
       @recipients = 'youremail@example.com',
       @subject = 'Backup Failed',
       @body = 'The backup for Database1 failed.';
   END CATCH;
   ```
2. **Set Up Database Mail**: Ensure Database Mail is configured in SQL Server for the sending of emails.
3. **Test the Setup**: Run your script to confirm emails are sent if the backup fails.

This will allow you to get immediate notifications for any issues. Let me know if you need more details on setting up Database Mail!
